# What `git archive` leaves behind when this project is vendored somewhere else.
#
# The aicoo website checks this project out as one folder under
# `tools/timeline-pptx-export/` (see docs/website-integration.md). It does not
# need the whole workshop, and it particularly does not need a second copy of
# the design system: the website already carries that in `.ds-sync/`, and two
# copies of a design system on one repository is exactly the thing that drifts.
#
# So `design-system/` is dropped from the archive — except the files this app
# genuinely compiles and verifies against, which are named back in below.
# `git archive HEAD | tar -x -C <dest>` therefore produces a folder that
# builds, and 155 files smaller.
#
# Nothing here affects this repository itself. The full design system stays
# checked in and is what `design-system/readme.md` calls the ground truth for
# the brand.

design-system/** export-ignore

# A blanket `**` excludes the directories on the way down as well, and a file
# inside an excluded directory is never reached — so every folder in the path
# of something kept has to be named back in before the file itself is.
design-system/tokens -export-ignore
design-system/components -export-ignore
design-system/components/core -export-ignore
design-system/components/forms -export-ignore
design-system/components/overlays -export-ignore

# --- kept: the stylesheet the app is actually built from -------------------
#
# `src/index.css` does `@import "../design-system/styles.css"`, which pulls the
# nine token files below. This is a build input, not reference material: remove
# it and `vite build` fails on a missing import, and every colour, radius,
# shadow and type step the app draws with goes with it.
design-system/styles.css -export-ignore
design-system/tokens/*.css -export-ignore

# --- kept: the four primitives `npm run check:design` reads -----------------
#
# `src/components/systemUi.ts` is a hand-made transcription of these into
# Tailwind classes, and checkDesignSystem.ts reads the originals at run time to
# prove the transcription has not drifted. Without them that check cannot run
# at all — and a check that cannot run is worse than one that fails, because
# nobody notices.
design-system/components/core/Button.jsx -export-ignore
design-system/components/forms/Input.jsx -export-ignore
design-system/components/forms/Checkbox.jsx -export-ignore
design-system/components/overlays/DropdownMenu.jsx -export-ignore

# --- kept: one page saying what the other 155 files were --------------------
design-system/readme.md -export-ignore
